# SRG-APP-000211-WSR-000030  -  CAT II
# Web server accounts accessing the directory tree, the shell, or other
# operating system functions and utilities must only be administrative
# accounts.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000211-WSR-000030
group:           V-206393
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      tested
cci:             CCI-001082
control_rev5:    SC-2

contribution:    Splunk Enterprise adopts the privileges of a named, non-root operating
                 system account for splunkd (SPLUNK_OS_USER), so the account that reaches
                 the directory tree and shell on behalf of the product is a dedicated
                 service account rather than a privileged one; role design additionally
                 bounds capability inheritance and delegation scope through importRoles and
                 grantableRoles.

governs:         splunk-launch.conf - Environment settings read before Splunk starts, including whether it
                 starts in FIPS mode.

check:           splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_OS_USER non_empty
check:           splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_OS_USER not_equals root
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_OS_USER https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/splunk-launch.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The inventory of operating system accounts on the host and whether any are
                 nonprivileged with access they do not need - operating system account
                 management
external:        Shell access and login capability for the splunkd service account -
                 operating system (shell assignment, PAM)
external:        File system ownership and permissions on the installation directory and
                 index paths - operating system
external:        Which Splunk roles hold capabilities that reach operating system functions
                 - assessed against SRG-APP-000211-WSR-000129 and SRG-APP-000246-WSR-000149

citation:        splunk-launch.conf.spec:97-103 (SPLUNK_OS_USER = <string> | <nonnegative
                 integer>; splunkd abandons root privileges immediately on start and
                 acquires this user's privileges); authorize.conf.spec:79-84 (importRoles);
                 authorize.conf.spec:86-92 (grantableRoles)
finding:         SPLUNK_OS_USER is unset or set to root, so splunkd retains privileges
                 beyond those needed for its role and the application makes no contribution
                 toward restricting the account that reaches the directory tree and shell.
